75129>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75129>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75129>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75129>>>// string information.
75129>>>//
75129>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75129>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75129>>>//       End_Procedure
75129>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75129>>>//                        bar title
75129>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75129>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75129>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75129>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75129>>>//                        is used.
75129>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75129>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75129>>>//
75129>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75129>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75129>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75129>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75129>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75129>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75129>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75129>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75129>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75129>>>//   end_procedure
75129>>>//   // end of file.
75129>>>
